WEBVTT

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:29.400
<i>The year was 1889.</i>

00:01:30.110 --> 00:01:34.320
<i>Jean, Nadia and King meet at the Paris World Exposition.</i>

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:36.820
<i>They traveled to Le Havre where Jean lives,</i>

00:01:37.490 --> 00:01:40.580
<i>but were attacked by a threesome in their multipurpose tank Gratan,</i>

00:01:40.580 --> 00:01:44.120
<i>who were after the Blue Water gem that Nadia possesses.</i>

00:01:44.330 --> 00:01:48.370
<i>Jean and his party barely escaped in Jean's self-constructed aircraft</i>

00:01:48.370 --> 00:01:52.130
<i>but an engine failure occurred and they splash landed in the ocean.</i>

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:57.130
<i>What is the secret that lies behind Nadia's Blue Water?</i>

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:29.620
Look, Jean, we're going to sink.

00:02:30.210 --> 00:02:33.710
That's why we've got to bail out the water as fast as we can.

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:38.880
Lucky cat.

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:47.060
Jean, what's that?

00:03:00.570 --> 00:03:01.660
It's a battleship!

00:03:06.740 --> 00:03:10.210
Man overboard! I see people adrift!

00:03:10.210 --> 00:03:11.540
Where?

00:03:14.210 --> 00:03:16.550
Stop engines! Change course 15 degrees to port!

00:03:22.930 --> 00:03:25.100
Lieutenant Commander, we're going to pick up those people.

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:25.930
Aye, aye, Sir!

00:03:29.730 --> 00:03:32.520
They've seen us! We're saved!

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:36.730
Ahoy!

00:03:39.070 --> 00:03:40.450
This is terrific!

00:03:41.740 --> 00:03:43.530
Ahoy!

00:03:44.070 --> 00:03:46.370
Is it just the two of you?

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:50.330
Yes, that's right! And a baby lion!

00:03:51.210 --> 00:03:53.170
All right! Understood!

00:03:53.170 --> 00:03:54.790
Can you come over here?

00:03:55.330 --> 00:03:57.090
Yes, of course!

00:03:57.090 --> 00:04:00.970
That's a funny looking boat. Doesn't look seaworthy.

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:03.220
It's not a boat. It's an aircraft!

00:04:03.380 --> 00:04:04.590
Aircraft?

00:04:04.590 --> 00:04:05.470
That's right.

00:04:05.470 --> 00:04:07.970
You mean a thing that can fly?

00:04:07.970 --> 00:04:09.470
Correct.

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:40.000
Please, remain seated.

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:42.010
Yes, Sir!

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:46.050
Welcome to my ship, the Abraham. My name is Captain Meville.

00:04:46.050 --> 00:04:48.260
This is my second in command, Lieutenant Commander Holland.

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:52.270
Thank you, Captain Meville, for rescuing us.

00:04:53.350 --> 00:04:57.270
There's no need to thank me. I only performed my duty.

00:04:58.230 --> 00:05:00.610
By the way, did you build that aircraft yourself?

00:05:00.730 --> 00:05:02.740
Yes, together with my uncle.

00:05:03.110 --> 00:05:05.360
I see. It shows a lot of ingenuity!

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:07.490
We're interested in building an air force.

00:05:07.490 --> 00:05:09.580
You won't mind if we look it over?

00:05:10.030 --> 00:05:10.700
Not at all!

00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:13.250
Good. Seaman!

00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:14.710
Yes, Sir!

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:20.630
Now tell me how you ended up drifting in the ocean.

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:22.260
Yes, Sir.

00:05:32.220 --> 00:05:36.980
Okay, I get the general picture. This trio was chasing you, right?

00:05:36.980 --> 00:05:38.100
Yes, Captain.

00:05:39.810 --> 00:05:43.280
I can't stand people who harass children like this.

00:05:45.110 --> 00:05:48.240
It appears as if somebody is talking about us.

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:51.280
We're so beautiful, it's only natural.

00:05:52.490 --> 00:05:57.620
Sanson, the word beautiful was made for me.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:03.050
No, you're wrong. It was meant for me.

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:10.140
We'll enter the 20th century soon, and they still spout nonsense.

00:06:10.140 --> 00:06:11.600
Shut up!

00:06:12.930 --> 00:06:18.770
You two! You'd better get busy and find that aircraft right now!

00:06:18.770 --> 00:06:19.900
Yes, Ma'am!

00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:23.400
The rain has stopped.

00:06:23.610 --> 00:06:25.400
Yes, it's a beautiful day.

00:06:27.740 --> 00:06:29.570
What's that?

00:06:29.570 --> 00:06:33.830
It's that American battleship sent to hunt down the sea monsters.

00:06:33.830 --> 00:06:34.490
I see.

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:39.250
A wise man stays away from danger.

00:06:42.250 --> 00:06:43.750
It's that airplane!

00:06:44.340 --> 00:06:45.420
We've found the Blue Water!

00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:46.920
Let me see.

00:06:46.920 --> 00:06:49.800
We'll be returning to France in three days.

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:51.890
We'll let you off when we reach France.

00:06:51.890 --> 00:06:53.890
Thank you, Captain Meville!

00:06:54.220 --> 00:06:57.180
This is my first time on a battleship.

00:06:57.180 --> 00:06:59.140
Would it be all right if I looked around?

00:06:59.560 --> 00:07:02.020
Of course, feel free to go where you please.

00:07:02.810 --> 00:07:04.400
Thanks a lot!

00:07:04.770 --> 00:07:05.980
Oh, Ayerton.

00:07:05.980 --> 00:07:06.480
Yes, Sir.

00:07:06.820 --> 00:07:08.490
Look after these children.

00:07:08.860 --> 00:07:09.610
Aye, Sir.

00:07:14.870 --> 00:07:18.540
You're not seriously thinking about attacking a battleship, are you?

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:22.790
Of course. I'll do anything to get my hands on that Blue Water.

00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:34.680
Ship approaching from the rear starboard side!

00:07:34.680 --> 00:07:35.720
What?

00:07:39.770 --> 00:07:41.980
It's that steel ship that the kids were talking about.

00:07:43.310 --> 00:07:47.020
Lt. Commander Holland, call the kids. Tell them we have guests.

00:07:47.020 --> 00:07:47.860
Roger!

00:07:48.070 --> 00:07:50.150
What? To the bridge?

00:07:50.150 --> 00:07:52.410
That's right. The Captain wants to see you.

00:07:52.410 --> 00:07:53.860
All right!

00:07:56.780 --> 00:07:59.040
This is a terrific ship!

00:08:01.660 --> 00:08:05.670
Say, Mr. Ayerton, what's the length of this ship?

00:08:09.090 --> 00:08:11.170
Actually, that's classified military data.

00:08:11.380 --> 00:08:12.430
Geez...

00:08:14.890 --> 00:08:17.050
Nadia, what's wrong?

00:08:17.050 --> 00:08:18.970
We're going up on the bridge. Aren't you excited?

00:08:18.970 --> 00:08:23.440
A warship is designed for killing people.

00:08:23.440 --> 00:08:24.690
How can you be interested?

00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:28.320
I guess that's true.

00:08:36.450 --> 00:08:37.830
Oh, here you are.

00:08:38.450 --> 00:08:40.200
Your guests have arrived.

00:08:46.290 --> 00:08:48.920
Look! It's Senorita Grandis and her men!

00:08:48.920 --> 00:08:50.920
They're still chasing us, even over the ocean.

00:08:51.170 --> 00:08:55.300
Right! Lt. Commander, fire two or three warning shots as a greeting.

00:08:55.300 --> 00:08:56.930
It's good training too.

00:08:56.930 --> 00:08:59.430
Aye, aye, Sir!
Main cannons, prepare for firing!

00:08:59.930 --> 00:09:01.770
Main cannons, prepare for firing!

00:09:05.770 --> 00:09:09.770
I think it'd be safer if we stay further away.

00:09:10.020 --> 00:09:13.570
Don't be foolish! We'll never be able to catch them!

00:09:13.570 --> 00:09:16.530
But what good is that if we get killed?

00:09:16.780 --> 00:09:22.410
Keep quiet! We have to take risks if we want to get that Blue Water!

00:09:33.590 --> 00:09:34.840
What's that thing?

00:09:34.840 --> 00:09:37.300
Those are the newest rotating turrets.

00:09:37.300 --> 00:09:39.970
They move the main cannons by hydraulics.

00:09:39.970 --> 00:09:41.850
They look quite fearsome.

00:09:44.180 --> 00:09:44.850
Oh, no!

00:09:49.150 --> 00:09:51.650
How can they start firing without giving us fair warning?

00:09:52.480 --> 00:09:54.690
No mercy for the bad guys!

00:09:58.950 --> 00:10:00.990
What a horrible ship!

00:10:00.990 --> 00:10:02.620
Sanson! Hanson! Start our counterattack!

00:10:02.620 --> 00:10:03.870
Aye, aye!

00:10:18.220 --> 00:10:19.340
Take this!

00:10:34.020 --> 00:10:36.070
My Gratan!

00:10:36.070 --> 00:10:37.950
My poor Gratan!

00:10:54.710 --> 00:10:57.550
We've got to surrender. Raise the white flag!

00:10:57.550 --> 00:10:58.760
You're sure?

00:10:58.760 --> 00:11:02.260
Of course I'm sure! Our lives come first!

00:11:11.100 --> 00:11:13.440
They should've surrendered at the start!

00:11:14.110 --> 00:11:14.690
Lieutenant Commander!

00:11:14.690 --> 00:11:15.570
Aye, Sir!

00:11:15.820 --> 00:11:19.900
Pick up the tank. We'll turn them in to the French police.

00:11:19.900 --> 00:11:20.400
Right, Sir!

00:11:21.910 --> 00:11:23.280
I feel sorry for them.

00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:41.070
That was good food!

00:12:41.490 --> 00:12:43.820
Have you finished already? You're fast.

00:12:43.820 --> 00:12:46.240
Yeah, I was pretty hungry.

00:12:46.240 --> 00:12:48.080
Besides, the food was very good.

00:12:48.080 --> 00:12:52.080
Thanks for the compliment. I'll tell the cook you said so.

00:12:52.080 --> 00:12:55.330
I thought you cooked the dinner for us.

00:12:55.830 --> 00:12:59.590
No, no! Not at all! I'm really a scientist.

00:12:59.590 --> 00:13:00.840
What? A scientist?

00:13:01.090 --> 00:13:05.010
I'm from America and I'm on a secret mission

00:13:05.010 --> 00:13:09.310
for the President of the United States. I'm Professor Ayerton,

00:13:09.310 --> 00:13:11.930
and I'm second only to the captain on this ship.

00:13:12.850 --> 00:13:15.600
A secret mission? That's why you're not in uniform!

00:13:15.890 --> 00:13:18.610
That's right. Now listen, Jean.

00:13:18.940 --> 00:13:21.610
All living things can be divided into two groups.

00:13:22.610 --> 00:13:25.360
Those that taste good and those that don't.

00:13:26.950 --> 00:13:29.580
Take this fish.

00:13:29.580 --> 00:13:31.660
This belongs to the group that tastes good!

00:13:37.830 --> 00:13:39.460
What's the matter, Nadia?

00:13:39.460 --> 00:13:41.210
You haven't taken a bite.

00:13:42.760 --> 00:13:43.960
I'm not hungry.

00:13:43.960 --> 00:13:47.180
What? You're not going to eat something as delicious as this?

00:13:47.180 --> 00:13:49.600
Nadia, I pity you.

00:13:49.600 --> 00:13:54.560
Life is composed of three actions: eating, sleeping and playing.

00:13:54.560 --> 00:14:00.900
How can you ignore something as important as this?

00:14:01.690 --> 00:14:06.990
Don't worry about me. I don't want to be happy if an animal must die.

00:14:06.990 --> 00:14:11.120
I see. You must be a vegetarian.

00:14:11.120 --> 00:14:12.410
What's that?

00:14:12.620 --> 00:14:16.710
You don't know? They don't eat fish or meat.

00:14:16.910 --> 00:14:18.710
I see, Nadia!

00:14:21.500 --> 00:14:23.340
But King eats meat.

00:14:26.760 --> 00:14:28.590
King is different.

00:14:34.520 --> 00:14:37.980
Now, don't you want to know about our secret mission?

00:14:37.980 --> 00:14:39.980
You're allowed to tell us?

00:14:39.980 --> 00:14:44.230
Only if you promise not to tell anyone else.

00:14:44.230 --> 00:14:45.980
Sure! We promise!

00:14:45.980 --> 00:14:47.740
This ship is on a mission to hunt down

00:14:47.740 --> 00:14:51.620
those giant sea monsters that are attacking ships all over the world.

00:14:51.620 --> 00:14:53.740
I know about that!

00:14:53.740 --> 00:14:55.080
You do?

00:14:55.080 --> 00:14:57.450
It was in the Paris newspapers.

00:15:00.960 --> 00:15:01.920
I see.

00:15:02.380 --> 00:15:07.420
But why is that a secret? Sea monsters don't read newspapers.

00:15:09.970 --> 00:15:11.550
I'm afraid that's a military secret.

00:15:11.970 --> 00:15:16.140
Against a big warship like this, the monsters don't stand a chance.

00:15:22.860 --> 00:15:26.860
This is the main mast! Sea monster sighted off the port side!

00:15:26.860 --> 00:15:28.570
Moving, bearing 104.

00:15:28.570 --> 00:15:30.320
All men to battle quarters!

00:15:30.320 --> 00:15:31.990
Roger! All men to general quarters!

00:15:32.360 --> 00:15:34.830
I repeat, to general quarters!

00:15:37.240 --> 00:15:41.290
All men to general quarters!

00:15:47.050 --> 00:15:48.590
We'd better go too.

00:15:56.600 --> 00:15:57.390
Over there!

00:16:00.810 --> 00:16:02.390
Found you at last!

00:16:02.640 --> 00:16:04.650
Only four days after leaving port.

00:16:05.020 --> 00:16:06.980
Lady Luck is with us!

00:16:06.980 --> 00:16:08.360
Open all cannon ports!

00:16:08.360 --> 00:16:10.860
Target giant sea monster off to port! Prepare for firing!

00:16:10.860 --> 00:16:11.900
Prepare for firing!

00:16:12.030 --> 00:16:13.360
No, you mustn't!

00:16:13.530 --> 00:16:15.240
What's that?

00:16:16.330 --> 00:16:20.200
It's a living being! You can't kill a poor animal!

00:16:21.910 --> 00:16:23.210
But I must.

00:16:23.580 --> 00:16:27.040
That thing has killed many sailors at sea.

00:16:27.540 --> 00:16:29.000
Get off the bridge!

00:16:30.670 --> 00:16:33.760
Distance and direction confirmed. All turrets trained on target!

00:16:33.760 --> 00:16:36.800
From ballistics to firing quarters, all conditions are go!

00:16:37.010 --> 00:16:39.100
All cannons, ready for continuous firing.

00:16:39.520 --> 00:16:42.810
Range to target: 12,000 meters. Speed: 30knots!

00:16:42.810 --> 00:16:45.230
30 knots? That's not possible!

00:16:45.230 --> 00:16:47.230
It can't be faster than my ship!

00:16:47.230 --> 00:16:49.320
All cannons ready for firing!

00:16:51.860 --> 00:16:53.700
Damn! Did it get away?

00:16:53.700 --> 00:16:57.070
That's funny. It looks as if it's being chased by something else.

00:16:57.530 --> 00:17:00.160
It's safe then? Thank goodness.

00:17:05.370 --> 00:17:07.210
Shut up! Get out of here!

00:17:17.760 --> 00:17:20.430
You talked too much. That's why we were chased out.

00:17:20.430 --> 00:17:24.480
But I couldn't let him kill it!

00:17:25.060 --> 00:17:26.270
Right, King?

00:17:28.980 --> 00:17:32.650
Geez, you're only thinking about your breakfast, I know.

00:17:33.030 --> 00:17:35.070
You understand what King is saying?

00:17:35.070 --> 00:17:37.700
Yes, and other animals too, a little.

00:17:38.990 --> 00:17:42.370
But I can't understand the sea beast's behavior.

00:17:42.950 --> 00:17:46.580
That sea monster is evil. That's why you can't understand it.

00:17:46.920 --> 00:17:49.540
Those beasts have been living in the sea since ancient times!

00:17:49.960 --> 00:17:53.300
Then men came along and started killing them off.

00:17:53.510 --> 00:17:55.380
What are you two arguing about?

00:17:55.920 --> 00:17:57.680
What happened to the sea monster?

00:17:58.510 --> 00:17:59.680
Didn't you see it?

00:18:00.680 --> 00:18:03.060
I was in the kitchen and didn't see a thing.

00:18:03.560 --> 00:18:05.680
What were you doing in the kitchen?

00:18:05.680 --> 00:18:09.100
I was preparing food for the sea beast.

00:18:10.230 --> 00:18:12.320
They eat sausages?

00:18:12.570 --> 00:18:15.320
That's a military secret too.

00:18:15.320 --> 00:18:18.570
Sausages? I can see King liking them, but...

00:18:21.280 --> 00:18:23.950
Everything is a military secret on board this ship.

00:18:23.950 --> 00:18:26.960
This is a military ship. It can't be helped.

00:18:26.960 --> 00:18:29.920
Look, if I do this, the sea monster will reappear.

00:18:36.510 --> 00:18:37.510
There it is!

00:18:37.510 --> 00:18:38.260
What the...

00:18:43.850 --> 00:18:45.020
There's another one!

00:18:45.310 --> 00:18:49.310
For a species to exist over tens of thousands of years,

00:18:49.310 --> 00:18:52.400
there must be male and female animals to bear babies.

00:18:52.940 --> 00:18:55.230
I see. They're mates!

00:18:55.230 --> 00:18:57.570
I can see that you're an expert on oceanography.

00:19:06.040 --> 00:19:07.620
We can't see them anymore.

00:19:07.620 --> 00:19:08.790
They've dived into the sea.

00:19:08.790 --> 00:19:13.540
They'll be back. Sea monsters are mammals and must surface for air.

00:19:13.710 --> 00:19:14.880
They're coming this way!

00:19:19.590 --> 00:19:23.550
Sea beast approaching from rear port quarter! Speed 32 knots!

00:19:23.850 --> 00:19:25.560
Haven't the main cannons got the range yet?

00:19:25.560 --> 00:19:27.810
It's not possible! It's too close!

00:19:27.810 --> 00:19:28.730
The secondary guns?

00:19:28.730 --> 00:19:30.060
Too late!

00:19:30.060 --> 00:19:31.310
What a mess!

00:19:33.310 --> 00:19:34.770
Look out! It's going to ram us!

00:19:46.160 --> 00:19:47.740
Lucky!

00:19:51.290 --> 00:19:54.920
Leakage in second compartment! Water entering third powder room!

00:19:54.920 --> 00:19:57.630
Ship is listing! Man the pumps!

00:19:57.630 --> 00:20:03.140
This just can't happen! This is a steel clad ship.

00:20:03.140 --> 00:20:07.640
How can a sea monster make a hole in it?

00:20:08.220 --> 00:20:11.140
The sea monster's on the starboard side and turning around!

00:20:11.140 --> 00:20:14.940
You monster! Starboard guns, begin firing! Get that thing!

00:20:23.780 --> 00:20:25.700
It made a metallic sound when the shells bounced off!

00:20:25.700 --> 00:20:27.620
Where's the other one?

00:20:28.830 --> 00:20:29.580
It's right below us!

00:20:33.870 --> 00:20:35.750
This one is chasing the other one!

00:20:40.760 --> 00:20:42.050
Are we going to sink?

00:20:42.050 --> 00:20:47.050
Don't worry. This is the newest battleship in the American navy!

00:20:47.050 --> 00:20:50.640
That's right! This ship was built with the newest techniques.

00:20:50.640 --> 00:20:52.810
This is the Abraham! How can it sink?

00:20:53.100 --> 00:20:55.310
I wonder if the sea beasts have been killed?

00:21:00.780 --> 00:21:01.860
A direct hit!

00:21:02.280 --> 00:21:04.200
It's still alive! It submerged!

00:21:04.200 --> 00:21:07.370
That's right! Run away quickly or you'll be killed!

00:21:14.830 --> 00:21:17.830
Sea monster coming from forward starboard quarter!

00:21:17.830 --> 00:21:19.840
Turn the wheel! Hard to starboard!

00:21:20.000 --> 00:21:21.130
Hard to starboard!

00:21:21.340 --> 00:21:25.130
Unbelievable! A direct hit from my main guns and it's still alive!

00:21:26.380 --> 00:21:28.890
Object approaching from front starboard quarter!

00:21:28.890 --> 00:21:29.600
What?

00:21:31.930 --> 00:21:32.770
What is it?

00:21:33.100 --> 00:21:33.770
It can't be!

00:21:34.180 --> 00:21:34.810
A torpedo?

00:21:52.870 --> 00:21:53.950
Nadia!

00:21:54.200 --> 00:21:54.960
Jean!

00:21:55.210 --> 00:21:56.370
Nadia!

00:21:59.840 --> 00:22:01.960
It's no use! The controls won't work!

00:22:01.960 --> 00:22:03.510
Ship is listing seven degrees to starboard.

00:22:03.510 --> 00:22:05.220
The main turrets won't rotate!

00:22:05.220 --> 00:22:06.970
Leaks in number three and five compartments!

00:22:06.970 --> 00:22:08.220
Number one turret out of commission!

00:22:08.220 --> 00:22:08.760
Captain!

00:22:08.760 --> 00:22:09.800
Get a hold of yourselves!

00:22:10.010 --> 00:22:12.060
Direct all efforts toward pumping water out of the starboard side!

00:22:33.790 --> 00:22:37.830
Nadia!

00:22:38.210 --> 00:22:39.670
Jean!

00:22:43.300 --> 00:22:44.840
Nadia!

00:22:47.590 --> 00:22:48.430
Are you all right?

00:22:48.430 --> 00:22:52.720
Yes, but, Jean, I can't find King!

00:22:52.720 --> 00:22:54.100
King?

00:22:54.430 --> 00:22:56.470
Yes, and the ship...

00:23:00.600 --> 00:23:02.900
They're not aware that we got swept overboard.

00:23:02.900 --> 00:23:03.980
But Ayerton should know.

00:23:04.480 --> 00:23:06.230
It's no use! Look!

00:23:06.780 --> 00:23:09.860
The steering controls have been damaged. They can't turn back.

00:23:10.490 --> 00:23:11.950
It looks that way.

00:23:13.370 --> 00:23:14.830
King?

00:23:19.660 --> 00:23:20.460
King!

00:23:21.630 --> 00:23:23.000
It's my airplane!

00:23:23.000 --> 00:23:24.090
King!

00:23:26.500 --> 00:23:28.590
King, King? Geez...

00:23:32.300 --> 00:23:35.390
But if that was really a torpedo,

00:23:36.060 --> 00:23:39.560
then what can that sea monster really be?
